WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.926
A NETFLIX SERIES

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.689
KOTARO LIVES ALONE

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:12.405
SHIMIZU APARTMENTS

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:15.450
WHO IS THE NEW RESIDENT?

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:16.576
Who are you?

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.037
Pleased to meet you. My name is Aota.

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:24.292
I'll be renting Room 103 downstairs
for a month, starting from today.

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:26.419
I see. It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:29.422
One month is rather short, isn't it?

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.841
It's work related.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:34.761
I'm on a business trip.
This is a greeting gift.

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:36.012
Please use it.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.972
Thank you for the gesture.

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:43.478
Kotaro Sato, do you live here by yourself?

00:01:43.561 --> 00:01:45.146
Yes. That is right.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:48.441
Well, Kotaro, I know I just met you,

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:50.235
but I have a little favor to ask.

00:01:50.318 --> 00:01:51.402
A favor?

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:54.322
Please! Just during
this business trip is fine.

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:56.407
Could you be my friend?

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.453
To tell the truth, I get lonely easily.

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:03.289
I get anxious when I'm by myself
in unfamiliar places.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.250
I don't mind.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:07.252
Wow, thank you!

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:10.505
Well, I'll go say hello
to the other residents.

00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:11.881
I'll come again.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:12.799
Okay.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.975
Oh, Sir Karino.
Are you back from shopping?

00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:25.436
You're already going to the bathhouse?
It's earlier than usual.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.814
Yes. I'm going with Sir Aota.

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:31.234
Is Mr. Aota the guy
who came to Room 103 today?

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:35.738
I promised I'd go with Sir Aota
while he was here.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.865
Really?

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:42.787
I didn't necessarily promise
to go together with you,

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.455
but thought I would mention it.

00:02:44.539 --> 00:02:46.416
Huh? What?

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.001
For that reason,

00:02:48.084 --> 00:02:50.628
I won't be going with you
to the bathhouse for a while.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.380
Okay, I get it.

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:53.840
Don't get jealous.

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:54.757
I'm not!

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.927
Also, Sir Aota will see me off and
pick me up from kindergarten

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.262
to know this area better.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.848
Therefore, you don't
need to do that either.

00:03:01.931 --> 00:03:04.225
Okay. Do whatever you like.

00:03:04.309 --> 00:03:05.185
Are you jealous?

00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:07.145
You're being an idiot!

00:03:07.228 --> 00:03:09.147
BATH

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:12.567
You always come with
Mr. Karino from Room 202?

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.484
Yes.

00:03:13.568 --> 00:03:16.237
Although I tell him
he doesn't have to come.

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:20.158
He really gets mad
when I go out by myself at night.

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:21.326
Really…

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:24.537
Kotaro, look!

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.332
A top-knot and beard.

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:32.170
Is that by chance,
Bubble Beard Tonosaman?!

00:03:32.253 --> 00:03:35.632
Oh, so you've done it before too.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.635
If you talk too much,
that ends up happening!

00:03:41.262 --> 00:03:45.141
Aho-uke is a local treat
from an area where I used to live.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.644
It is my favorite snack!

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:51.356
I got these from a coworker,
but I'm glad you like them.

00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:54.067
I also like Aho-uke.

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:57.070
Mmm, it's good!

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:58.696
What a coincidence!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.698
I used to eat them like that too!

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:04.077
Really? I guess we're like-minded.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.453
That's true!

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:09.749
By the way,
it's raining really hard outside.

00:04:09.832 --> 00:04:11.042
I know!

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:12.752
Ta-da!

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.004
Thanks to the raindrops,

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:18.383
even bowls, pots and pans
can become instruments!

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:20.343
Hmm?

00:04:24.138 --> 00:04:24.973
It's nothing.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.104
Mr. Karino!

00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:34.440
Oh, Mr. Aota. Thanks.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.402
Thank you for taking Kotaro
to the bathhouse

00:04:37.485 --> 00:04:39.737
and going with him
to kindergarten every day.

00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:40.947
Not at all,

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.574
I asked Kotaro to keep me company.

00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:46.327
Besides, you've been with him
all this time.

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:49.330
Mr. Karino,

00:04:49.414 --> 00:04:52.041
how much do you know about Kotaro?

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.501
About what?

00:04:53.584 --> 00:04:56.254
Why he started living by himself,

00:04:56.337 --> 00:04:58.256
about his parents and finances.

00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:01.634
I asked Kotaro, but he didn't answer.

00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:03.594
So you ask me?

00:05:03.678 --> 00:05:05.972
Yes, I thought you'd know
since you're close--

00:05:06.055 --> 00:05:08.725
- Even if I knew, I wouldn't tell you.
- Huh?

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:12.353
You shouldn't dig into things
he doesn't want to talk about.

00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:16.441
Yes, you're right. Sorry about that.

00:05:18.443 --> 00:05:20.445
Hello, this is Aota.

00:05:21.237 --> 00:05:23.156
I apologize for the late call.

00:05:23.239 --> 00:05:26.492
I'll follow up on the details later,

00:05:26.576 --> 00:05:27.827
but there's no mistake.

00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:29.495
I found him.

00:05:30.246 --> 00:05:31.622
Your son.

00:05:45.762 --> 00:05:47.722
The way that doorbell's ringing…

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.975
What's the meaning of this?

00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:54.645
Karino! What the hell is with that guy?
Huh?!

00:05:54.729 --> 00:05:55.688
That guy?

00:05:55.772 --> 00:05:59.108
Aota! From 103!

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:03.654
How is he so close to Kotaro
when he just came here?

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:05.698
Seems he hangs out at Kotaro's too!

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:07.033
I'm so jealous!

00:06:07.116 --> 00:06:11.287
Mr. Tamaru, what do you think
when you see Mr. Aota?

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.873
Huh? Isn't it obvious?

00:06:13.956 --> 00:06:16.417
That guy is sketchy.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:17.335
Huh?

00:06:17.418 --> 00:06:20.296
I felt it when he came to say hi.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.216
There's something fishy about him.

00:06:23.299 --> 00:06:26.677
But, he gets along so well with Kotaro!

00:06:26.761 --> 00:06:30.598
I don't want to intrude
and have Kotaro hate me!

00:06:30.681 --> 00:06:32.016
- Well,
- Huh?

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.018
actually, yesterday, Mr. Aota…

00:06:39.107 --> 00:06:40.233
Coming.

00:06:40.316 --> 00:06:42.402
Is it time to go to the bathhouse?

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:48.574
Hello. I'm Tamaru from next door.

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:50.910
What's going on?--

00:06:50.993 --> 00:06:54.580
Seems that you've been snooping
for information about Kotaro, huh?

00:06:55.164 --> 00:06:57.041
You're a detective, right?

00:06:57.125 --> 00:06:59.836
What's this about so suddenly? I'm not.

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:04.632
As someone who works in shady business,
you know what this means.

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:07.218
I won't tell anyone else. Speak up.

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:11.514
I've seen this scene in a movie…

00:07:13.057 --> 00:07:14.725
It's his father.

00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:15.768
Huh?

00:07:15.852 --> 00:07:18.104
The father wanted to find his son.

00:07:18.187 --> 00:07:20.606
I came here at his father's request.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:21.649
Huh?

00:07:21.732 --> 00:07:23.693
As a result of my investigations,

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:28.239
I found out that Kotaro moved here
so his father wouldn't find him.

00:07:28.322 --> 00:07:33.744
Additionally, a restraining order
was placed on the father for Kotaro.

00:07:33.828 --> 00:07:36.998
Well, I think you'd have guessed
without me saying anything.

00:07:37.707 --> 00:07:41.210
And you're saying that
you'll tell the father where he is?

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:44.464
Yes, I'll report it. It is my job.

00:07:44.547 --> 00:07:46.132
Well, as I said,

00:07:46.215 --> 00:07:48.384
Kotaro is protected by the law.

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:49.844
Mr. Tamaru!

00:07:49.927 --> 00:07:52.972
So once the job's done,
it's none of your concern?

00:07:53.055 --> 00:07:54.432
Yes, that's right.

00:07:54.515 --> 00:07:55.850
But, with all due respect,

00:07:56.434 --> 00:08:00.563
do you think a small child like Kotaro

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:04.066
is happy like this, living by himself?

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.403
You all are just tenants
of the same building.

00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:10.114
You don't have the right to interfere.

00:08:10.198 --> 00:08:11.657
Sir Aota, the bathhouse--

00:08:11.741 --> 00:08:14.076
You bastard! What did you just say?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.997
What are you doing, Sir Tamaru?

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.874
Don't bully Sir Aota!

00:08:23.753 --> 00:08:26.088
Are you okay, Sir Aota?

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:28.216
Well, let's go to the bathhouse.

00:08:28.299 --> 00:08:29.175
Okay.

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:37.433
Do you think a small child like Kotaro
is happy like this, living by himself?

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:52.323
A week has already passed since I started
going to the bathhouse with you, Kotaro.

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:54.283
Time really flies.

00:08:54.825 --> 00:08:58.204
It's a short time,
but let's keep in touch, okay?

00:08:58.788 --> 00:09:00.039
Sir Aota.

00:09:00.122 --> 00:09:01.249
What?

00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:07.171
Will you tell my father that I live here?

00:09:16.305 --> 00:09:19.517
I DON'T NEED HELP/I WANT TO BECOME STRONG

00:09:20.101 --> 00:09:23.104
Now, Sir Karino, let's go to kindergarten.

00:09:24.188 --> 00:09:26.774
- Huh?
- You haven't come with me for a while.

00:09:26.857 --> 00:09:28.651
You must have been lonely.

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:30.528
Wait a second. Where's Mr. Aota?

00:09:30.611 --> 00:09:32.530
Sir Aota is not here.

00:09:32.613 --> 00:09:34.365
He seems to have gotten urgent work

00:09:34.448 --> 00:09:36.826
and left the apartment early this morning.

00:09:38.369 --> 00:09:40.621
What?! He left?!

00:09:41.414 --> 00:09:43.332
Did Aota rush to tell the father

00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:46.210
because we caught him?

00:09:46.711 --> 00:09:50.256
Yeah, sorry. I ran back
from the kindergarten at full speed.

00:09:50.339 --> 00:09:52.216
We don't have time!

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.176
Hey, what's going on?

00:09:55.303 --> 00:09:56.304
So scary…

00:09:56.387 --> 00:09:57.680
Who are they?

00:09:58.848 --> 00:10:01.517
Listen! We can't leave Kotaro's side,

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:04.937
not even at kindergarten!

00:10:05.021 --> 00:10:08.941
Isn't Mr. Aota awful,
even if he's doing his job?

00:10:09.025 --> 00:10:12.069
He knows Kotaro will be in danger
if he reports him, right?

00:10:12.153 --> 00:10:15.906
I've seen him
being friendly with Kotaro before…

00:10:16.824 --> 00:10:20.077
but that means
he didn't think anything of Kotaro.

00:10:20.161 --> 00:10:22.455
Yeah, that cold-blooded jerk!

00:10:22.538 --> 00:10:24.248
I wanna do it too!

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.878
Kotaro, come over here already!

00:10:30.504 --> 00:10:32.715
What is the meaning of this?

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:35.176
You're in danger right now, Kotaro!

00:10:35.259 --> 00:10:37.178
So we're protecting you!

00:10:37.762 --> 00:10:38.721
Protecting?

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:43.309
I don't understand,
I can protect my body on my own.

00:10:43.392 --> 00:10:47.146
But, it's safer
being with us as well, right?

00:10:47.229 --> 00:10:49.649
That being said, don't worry about it.

00:11:00.576 --> 00:11:01.410
Huh?

00:11:02.286 --> 00:11:04.622
Didn't I say I don't need protection?

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.959
Don't treat me like a weakling!

00:11:09.043 --> 00:11:10.294
Kotaro!

00:11:11.295 --> 00:11:13.547
No way, did we upset him?

00:11:13.631 --> 00:11:17.677
Did we do something that bad to Kotaro?

00:11:25.226 --> 00:11:26.477
Do you have a minute?

00:11:27.436 --> 00:11:30.314
What is your business?
You're interrupting my sit-ups.

00:11:31.816 --> 00:11:33.067
Are you upset?

00:11:35.319 --> 00:11:36.946
I don't need your protection!

00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:39.615
You know,

00:11:39.699 --> 00:11:41.992
you don't have to say it
if you don't want to,

00:11:43.452 --> 00:11:45.705
but why did you want to live by yourself?

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:48.582
To become stronger.

00:11:48.666 --> 00:11:49.500
Stronger?

00:11:50.793 --> 00:11:51.627
Is that so

00:11:52.128 --> 00:11:54.171
you can continue to live on your own?

00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:55.131
No.

00:11:55.214 --> 00:11:56.882
- Then why--
- Isn't that enough?

00:11:56.966 --> 00:11:58.718
I am busy right now!

00:12:00.636 --> 00:12:05.391
Karino, when you went to kindergarten
with Kotaro today, how was he?

00:12:06.016 --> 00:12:08.352
I tried to reason with him.

00:12:08.436 --> 00:12:12.148
He said he's only going with me
because we promised and he had no choice.

00:12:12.231 --> 00:12:14.984
He didn't even look me in the eye.

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:19.572
If he's not trying to get stronger
so he can live by himself,

00:12:20.156 --> 00:12:24.368
I wonder if it's in order to
protect himself when his dad comes.

00:12:24.452 --> 00:12:26.078
If that's the case,

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.748
I feel really bad for Kotaro.

00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:35.880
Aota, you jerk! Where the hell did you go?

00:12:36.422 --> 00:12:38.090
To report to my client.

00:12:38.174 --> 00:12:41.093
- You bastard!
- Whoa! Calm down, Tamaru!

00:12:41.886 --> 00:12:44.388
Did you really tell him his whereabouts?

00:12:44.472 --> 00:12:47.141
Of course, that was my main objective.

00:12:47.808 --> 00:12:48.642
Kotaro.

00:12:50.811 --> 00:12:53.481
Sir Aota, you've come back.

00:12:53.564 --> 00:12:56.358
Yes, I've come back.
Are you going out now?

00:12:56.442 --> 00:12:59.945
Yes. I am going to play with Sir Takuya
at the nearby park.

00:13:00.029 --> 00:13:02.198
May I go with you?

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:03.532
That's fine.

00:13:04.116 --> 00:13:06.118
I'd like everyone else to go too.

00:13:06.202 --> 00:13:08.913
I'd like to continue sharing my story.

00:13:12.333 --> 00:13:16.504
How did his father react
when he found out where he was?

00:13:17.004 --> 00:13:18.798
He was pretty excited.

00:13:19.298 --> 00:13:21.967
He might make his move today or tomorrow.

00:13:22.051 --> 00:13:23.052
Oh no…

00:13:23.135 --> 00:13:24.804
Shit. What do we do?

00:13:24.887 --> 00:13:26.972
Should we help Kotaro escape?

00:13:27.056 --> 00:13:29.266
No, there's no need for that.

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:30.226
What?

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:34.563
Because I haven't told Kotaro's father
his real address.

00:13:34.647 --> 00:13:35.648
What?!

00:13:35.731 --> 00:13:38.192
I gave him the address
of a vacant apartment

00:13:38.275 --> 00:13:40.694
in a building my coworker owns.

00:13:41.237 --> 00:13:44.782
Therefore, Kotaro will not
be in any danger.

00:13:45.366 --> 00:13:46.700
Why did you do that?

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:55.125
I went through a lot
when I was young as well.

00:13:55.209 --> 00:13:57.211
I may have a job like this,

00:13:57.711 --> 00:14:00.047
but I do still have a heart.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.843
You went through the trouble
to fool us too.

00:14:04.844 --> 00:14:10.599
However, Kotaro knew that
I was someone connected to his father.

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:11.517
What?

00:14:12.142 --> 00:14:14.061
He figured it out

00:14:14.144 --> 00:14:17.147
when I played the games

00:14:17.231 --> 00:14:19.483
his father informed me he liked.

00:14:19.567 --> 00:14:22.820
Those memories must have left
a deep impression.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.613
I let my guard down.

00:14:25.531 --> 00:14:29.410
When he cornered me about it,
I kept denying it.

00:14:29.493 --> 00:14:30.661
Then…

00:14:32.496 --> 00:14:34.874
Sir Aota, I beg you.

00:14:34.957 --> 00:14:39.420
Please hold off on telling my father
until I am stronger.

00:14:40.129 --> 00:14:40.963
In the end,

00:14:41.046 --> 00:14:44.133
I could only say, "Okay."

00:14:44.216 --> 00:14:45.718
Stronger?

00:14:45.801 --> 00:14:48.846
So it's in order to protect himself
from his dad's violence?

00:14:48.929 --> 00:14:50.180
Ow!

00:14:50.973 --> 00:14:53.350
You should not scream over just an ant.

00:14:53.434 --> 00:14:55.644
You will look like a weakling.

00:14:55.728 --> 00:14:59.857
Don't say the same thing as my dad.
What's with saying, "Get stronger?"

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.652
Yes. Your father
is saying the right thing.

00:15:03.736 --> 00:15:06.155
You don't even live with your father.

00:15:06.238 --> 00:15:07.656
What do you know?

00:15:08.198 --> 00:15:10.743
If you remain a weakling, Sir Takuya,

00:15:10.826 --> 00:15:14.830
there may come a time you can no longer
live with your parents, like me.

00:15:14.914 --> 00:15:16.874
Oh, why is that?

00:15:16.957 --> 00:15:19.293
If I hadn't been a weakling,

00:15:19.376 --> 00:15:21.795
my father wouldn't have become a bad guy.

00:15:22.463 --> 00:15:27.051
Therefore, if I become strong,
I can live with my father again.

00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:32.222
He thinks his dad became a bad guy
because he was a weakling?

00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:37.895
"My parents don't love me,

00:15:37.978 --> 00:15:41.482
and they abuse me
because I'm worthless and weak."

00:15:42.274 --> 00:15:44.151
I used to think that too.

00:15:44.735 --> 00:15:47.321
I thought I was wrong, not my father.

00:15:47.404 --> 00:15:48.864
So Kotaro thinks that,

00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:52.117
if he gets stronger, his father
will love him and not abuse him,

00:15:52.826 --> 00:15:55.287
and that they can live together again.

00:15:56.163 --> 00:15:58.082
Although, I don't think it's likely

00:15:58.165 --> 00:16:01.543
his father will understand his feelings.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:06.048
Hey, let's race.

00:16:06.131 --> 00:16:06.966
Huh?

00:16:07.466 --> 00:16:09.093
Race to the apartments!

00:16:09.176 --> 00:16:10.970
Hey! You are cheating!

00:16:12.179 --> 00:16:14.473
What is Karino doing?

00:16:17.476 --> 00:16:18.811
Did I seriously lose?

00:16:18.894 --> 00:16:22.523
I work out every day.
How can you win against me?

00:16:23.524 --> 00:16:27.903
Hey, do you want to get stronger
all by yourself?

00:16:27.987 --> 00:16:31.407
Yes. If I can do everything by myself,
I can be come stronger!

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:37.454
Did you know this? Strength is easier
to attain when you have a rival!

00:16:37.538 --> 00:16:38.831
What?!

00:16:38.914 --> 00:16:42.668
Even now, I was able to get the strength
to run that distance!

00:16:42.751 --> 00:16:43.752
So!

00:16:45.045 --> 00:16:46.630
Let's get stronger together!

00:16:48.757 --> 00:16:51.385
Yes! Then let's get stronger together!

00:16:52.177 --> 00:16:54.888
Alright. Sorry though,
could I have some water?

00:16:54.972 --> 00:16:56.473
That is quite pathetic.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:04.940
Hey, Karino. You know
that won't solve the problem, right?

00:17:05.607 --> 00:17:06.483
Yeah.

00:17:07.026 --> 00:17:09.945
So until the day he realizes he's wrong,

00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:14.533
I want him to get a little stronger,
both physically and mentally.

00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:17.578
So he can overcome his hardship.

00:17:21.331 --> 00:17:23.292
Look at you acting so cool!

00:17:23.375 --> 00:17:25.544
Don't steal the lines I wanted to say!

00:17:25.627 --> 00:17:26.920
Huh? Sorry.

00:17:27.004 --> 00:17:30.174
But, Karino, you really are out of shape.

00:17:30.799 --> 00:17:35.054
Since Sir Kario is physically weak,
I will serve him some protein.

00:17:37.765 --> 00:17:39.975
Do you know about the flower marks?

00:17:40.059 --> 00:17:40.893
What?

00:17:40.976 --> 00:17:43.020
It's the mark a teacher puts on

00:17:43.103 --> 00:17:45.439
elementary school tests
when kids get a 100.

00:17:45.522 --> 00:17:48.984
My son got them so many times.

00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:51.987
Mr. Kaneshiro, you have a son?

00:17:52.071 --> 00:17:54.573
Yeah, he's with my ex-wife.

00:17:54.656 --> 00:17:59.203
Come to think of it, the rift between
my son and I started around that time.

00:17:59.286 --> 00:18:01.080
More importantly,

00:18:01.163 --> 00:18:05.334
can you focus on acting like
a client's son to scam some money?

00:18:05.417 --> 00:18:07.086
I know.

00:18:07.169 --> 00:18:09.671
The next one is an old couple's house.

00:18:09.755 --> 00:18:10.589
Hello?

00:18:10.672 --> 00:18:13.092
Oh, Mom? It's me. Me!

00:18:13.175 --> 00:18:15.135
I'm in trouble. Please help!

00:18:15.219 --> 00:18:16.428
What's the problem?

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:20.099
A kid's voice?
Is he the old couple's grandson?

00:18:20.182 --> 00:18:22.226
The residents of this house are out.

00:18:22.309 --> 00:18:25.145
I am an acquaintance
who was asked to watch the house.

00:18:25.229 --> 00:18:27.773
Well, I guess that's not a problem.

00:18:27.856 --> 00:18:32.027
Man, I'm in a rush.
Do you know what time they'll be back?

00:18:32.111 --> 00:18:35.155
Oh, you're in a hurry? Sounds tough.

00:18:35.239 --> 00:18:36.240
Yeah.

00:18:36.323 --> 00:18:37.616
- I see.
- Yeah.

00:18:39.493 --> 00:18:41.745
So, when will they come back?

00:18:41.829 --> 00:18:43.497
Oh, sorry.

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:46.041
I think they will come back
in about five minutes.

00:18:46.125 --> 00:18:48.544
Got it. Then I'll call back, okay?

00:18:51.922 --> 00:18:53.924
Hello. It is I.

00:18:54.716 --> 00:18:56.635
They haven't come back, right?

00:18:56.718 --> 00:18:57.845
They haven't yet.

00:18:57.928 --> 00:19:00.889
They should be home in about five minutes.

00:19:01.598 --> 00:19:03.225
Yes. It is I.

00:19:03.308 --> 00:19:05.519
They will surely be home
in about five minutes.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.272
It is I again.

00:19:08.355 --> 00:19:12.109
Are your parents really coming home soon?

00:19:12.192 --> 00:19:13.652
Actually, I do not know.

00:19:13.735 --> 00:19:15.487
What's with this brat?

00:19:15.571 --> 00:19:18.532
Could you tell me
what you would like to say?

00:19:18.615 --> 00:19:22.494
I am in kindergarten,
but I can listen to what you have to say.

00:19:22.578 --> 00:19:25.414
What?! They're having
a kindergartener watch the house?

00:19:25.497 --> 00:19:27.624
It is nothing at all.

00:19:27.708 --> 00:19:30.127
Since I am also living by myself.

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:31.753
Living by yourself?

00:19:32.629 --> 00:19:34.923
What about your daddy and mommy?

00:19:35.007 --> 00:19:36.633
They are not with me.

00:19:36.717 --> 00:19:40.387
Seriously? Terrible parents. Well,

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:43.348
I can't say anything about others.

00:19:43.432 --> 00:19:45.309
Go! Number 4!

00:19:45.392 --> 00:19:48.020
Number 4! What are you doing? C'mon, go!

00:19:48.103 --> 00:19:50.230
Are you in some big trouble?

00:19:50.314 --> 00:19:54.109
Well, I made a little mistake at work.

00:19:54.193 --> 00:19:56.820
I need a considerable amount of money.

00:19:56.904 --> 00:19:58.572
Is this about money?

00:19:58.655 --> 00:20:02.242
If you're talking about money,
I'm good at saving it.

00:20:02.326 --> 00:20:04.786
The other day, to get the cheapest eggs,

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:08.207
I went to a grocery store
that was 40 minutes away.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:10.667
Is that not something? Amazing, right?

00:20:12.294 --> 00:20:14.004
Yeah.

00:20:14.796 --> 00:20:19.176
More importantly,
do you plan to relay my message?

00:20:19.259 --> 00:20:24.264
Sorry, I just wanted
to talk to you a little bit.

00:20:24.348 --> 00:20:26.600
What the heck. I'm hanging up--

00:20:26.683 --> 00:20:31.313
Your voice sounded like my father
when he was kind.

00:20:34.733 --> 00:20:36.652
Also, I want to ask this of you.

00:20:38.237 --> 00:20:42.908
I want you to tell me, "You're doing
a great job. You're fantastic."

00:20:45.244 --> 00:20:48.997
I really was an awful father.

00:20:51.041 --> 00:20:53.627
You're doing a great job.

00:20:54.836 --> 00:20:56.129
How fantastic…

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.174
Okay.

00:20:59.675 --> 00:21:01.009
My thanks to you!

00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:09.434
I want to live a "flower mark" life!

00:21:09.518 --> 00:21:12.604
Mr. Kaneshiro,
why don't you quit this line of work?

00:21:12.688 --> 00:21:14.314
Welcome back,
Sir and Lady Landlords.

00:21:14.398 --> 00:21:17.192
Was it fun going shopping with your son?

00:21:21.196 --> 00:21:23.573
Your business trip is almost done.

00:21:23.657 --> 00:21:26.076
Yeah. One month goes by fast, huh?

00:21:28.161 --> 00:21:29.705
My underwear is

00:21:29.788 --> 00:21:31.623
gone!

00:21:32.749 --> 00:21:35.377
What kind of underpants?
What color and shape?

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.462
What do you mean your underwear is gone?

00:21:37.546 --> 00:21:40.465
I put them in my basket,
thinking I'd wash them later.

00:21:40.549 --> 00:21:42.718
When I woke up from a nap, they were gone!

00:21:42.801 --> 00:21:44.553
Unwashed underwear?!

00:21:44.636 --> 00:21:47.639
Kotaro being intrigued is so cute!

00:21:47.723 --> 00:21:49.933
Would you like for me to investigate?

00:21:50.017 --> 00:21:53.020
Oh, right. You are a detective, Mr. Aota.

00:21:53.103 --> 00:21:54.813
I will help too!

00:21:54.896 --> 00:21:56.481
Detective Kotaro!

00:21:56.565 --> 00:21:57.774
Yay!

00:21:57.858 --> 00:21:59.860
Then, please pardon me.

00:22:06.074 --> 00:22:08.160
Is the veranda window always open?

00:22:08.243 --> 00:22:10.370
I open it sometimes for airflow…

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:19.254
There's something that looks like
underwear on Mr. Karino's patio.

00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:20.255
Huh?

00:22:21.798 --> 00:22:24.801
No, this is wrong! It's not me!

00:22:24.885 --> 00:22:27.637
You're the worst! Another turn off!

00:22:27.721 --> 00:22:30.849
I thought you'd do that at some point,
but you finally did.

00:22:30.932 --> 00:22:32.726
Huh? Hey, you traitor!

00:22:34.186 --> 00:22:35.729
It's the work of a cat.

00:22:35.812 --> 00:22:36.688
What?

00:22:36.772 --> 00:22:39.775
The cat entered from the open window,

00:22:39.858 --> 00:22:41.109
took the underwear,

00:22:41.193 --> 00:22:43.487
then crossed to Mr. Karino's patio,

00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:45.781
tore up the underwear and left it there.

00:22:46.323 --> 00:22:48.325
I'm pretty sure that cat is the culprit.

00:22:48.408 --> 00:22:49.576
It's Sir Hanbe!

00:22:49.659 --> 00:22:52.162
There was a trace of the same color fur,

00:22:52.245 --> 00:22:55.540
and cats sometimes react
to human pheromones.

00:22:55.624 --> 00:22:58.168
Oh, I see. So it was the cat.

00:22:58.251 --> 00:23:00.045
See, I said it wasn't me!

00:23:00.128 --> 00:23:02.756
That's amazing. Excellent detective work!

00:23:02.839 --> 00:23:06.009
My work isn't something to be praised.

00:23:06.093 --> 00:23:08.720
At times, I deceive people without qualm.

00:23:09.304 --> 00:23:10.222
Deceive?

00:23:13.725 --> 00:23:16.853
Oh, Kotaro. That's a lot of bags.

00:23:16.937 --> 00:23:19.773
It's an emergency.
There are no more boxes.

00:23:19.856 --> 00:23:20.732
Boxes?

00:23:20.816 --> 00:23:24.277
Yes. The boxes
have disappeared from my room.

00:23:24.361 --> 00:23:27.197
I want you to help me investigate.

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:30.534
I'll be waiting here. I'm counting on you.

00:23:31.284 --> 00:23:33.286
I don't really get it, but…

00:23:36.081 --> 00:23:36.998
Ink?

00:23:37.916 --> 00:23:39.543
Boxes?

00:23:39.626 --> 00:23:44.089
I took them from his place for a reason,
but they've disappeared.

00:23:44.172 --> 00:23:46.007
Huh? This perfume is…

00:23:46.508 --> 00:23:48.343
Oh, the boxes.

00:23:48.427 --> 00:23:51.721
I took them from Karino's place
for a reason, but they disappeared…

00:23:52.305 --> 00:23:55.392
That's right,
these sunglasses were dropped.

00:23:55.475 --> 00:23:57.978
What? Those are my sunglasses.

00:23:58.061 --> 00:24:01.648
I took the boxes for a reason,
but they disappeared.

00:24:01.731 --> 00:24:05.485
You took them, didn't you?
I bet that's it! It's fishy.

00:24:05.569 --> 00:24:07.362
No, that's incorrect.

00:24:08.238 --> 00:24:10.824
Stop babbling and show me your room.

00:24:10.907 --> 00:24:12.659
Okay, understood.

00:24:14.578 --> 00:24:16.413
We did it!

00:24:16.955 --> 00:24:19.374
Huh, why is everyone here?

00:24:19.458 --> 00:24:21.418
Kotaro planned this.

00:24:21.501 --> 00:24:25.589
A "surprise farewell party
to make the duped Sir Aota happy!"

00:24:26.214 --> 00:24:27.299
Farewell party?

00:24:27.966 --> 00:24:30.510
What did you think about my prank?

00:24:30.594 --> 00:24:32.053
Well…

00:24:32.554 --> 00:24:35.348
Oh, a box! Is it the box?

00:24:35.432 --> 00:24:37.726
Yes. It is your present.

00:24:37.809 --> 00:24:39.436
Huh? Oh, thank--

00:24:39.519 --> 00:24:40.937
By the way, Sir Aota,

00:24:41.021 --> 00:24:42.647
at the beginning,

00:24:42.731 --> 00:24:46.067
was being my friend just part of your job?

00:24:46.151 --> 00:24:50.780
However, your work for my father
has been done for a while now.

00:24:50.864 --> 00:24:55.243
Even so, you continued to be friends
with me until today, Sir Aota.

00:24:55.952 --> 00:24:59.164
In other words, according to my reasoning,

00:24:59.247 --> 00:25:03.043
you and I are not just work friends,

00:25:03.126 --> 00:25:05.795
but real friends.

00:25:09.758 --> 00:25:12.135
Is my reasoning incorrect?

00:25:13.178 --> 00:25:14.971
A magnifying glass…

00:25:17.766 --> 00:25:19.017
Impressive work,

00:25:19.726 --> 00:25:22.020
Detective Kotaro.
